config COBS
    bool "COBS framing library"
    default y
    help
        Enable the COBS (Consistent Overhead Byte Stuffing) framing library.

config COBS_LOG_LEVEL
    int "COBS log level"
    default 2
    depends on COBS
    help
        Set the log level for the COBS module:
        0: Off
        1: Error
        2: Warning
        3: Info
        4: Debug

config COBS_FRAME_SIZE
    int "COBS on-wire fragment size"
    default 244
    depends on COBS
    help
        Size (in bytes) of a single encoded COBS fragment on the transport
        wire. Also sizes the per-context RX accumulator and TX scratch
        buffers. This is NOT the maximum message size — large messages are
        split across multiple fragments. For BLE NUS, this must be <=
        (negotiated ATT MTU - 3) so each fragment fits in one notification;
        with CONFIG_BT_L2CAP_TX_MTU=247 the correct value is 244. Do not
        change unless the BLE MTU changes.

config COBS_MAX_MESSAGE_SIZE
    int "COBS maximum reassembled message size"
    default 4096
    depends on COBS
    help
        Upper bound (in bytes) on a single reassembled user message. Sizes
        the per-context reassembly buffer inside each cobs_framing_t. The
        framing library splits outgoing messages larger than one fragment
        into as many COBS fragments as required (capped at 255 fragments
        per message). Set this to the largest CFL payload the application
        will ever exchange on one transport. Each active framing context
        reserves this much DRAM, so budget accordingly.
